stdin	-
argv	exhaustive 6
why	the workhorse run (Lon 2026-10-01, the grammar-based generator demo): every calculator expression of at most 6 tokens, 12124 lines, run ONCE at wall clock and graded byte for byte against the oracle (24 s under the stock iconx, 14.8 s under SCRIP); the sample is the random walk, one thousand expressions from seed 1; the exhaustive walk is laid out with the alternation bars at the line starts, which the patched oracle reads as SCRIP does
